                <pb facs="0342" n="28" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg28"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/52</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Page</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1914-08-01T19:00:00+00:00">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">August 1, 1914, 7 p.m.</hi>
                    </date>
                    <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 9 p.m.</hi>] </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>Your July 31, 5 p.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d57-f1"/>. No absolutely conclusive
                    [developments?] but all to-day’s news points to Russia and Germany becoming
                    involved. Communication becomes more difficult from Germany and the telephone
                    from Paris is cut off. Increasing crowds of Americans are flocking from the
                    Continent. The canceling of all German transatlantic ships causes the detention
                    here of many travelers. There will be many cases of want presented to the
                    Embassy forthwith. Have you instructions for their assistance?</p>
                <p>There is yet no financial stringency. Brown Shipley report they can not longer
                    negotiate checks on American or Continental bankers.</p>
                <p>British Admiralty expect a general war and British troops are being concentrated
                    on the North Sea coast.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Page</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
